    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a clear emphasis on exploiting favorable pitching matchups for our top-tier talent. The strongest plays of the day are **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (72.18) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (72.01), both of whom benefit significantly from facing softer pitching opponents. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** faces Dobnak (xERA 4.62) with a massive 15% skill-based boost, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** sees a 14% platoon edge against King, making them the engines of our offense. **Sam Antonacci** (63.14) and **Miguel Vargas** (62.46) also represent high-value starts; both are positioned to capitalize on Ober\u2019s vulnerable 4.79 xERA, with **Antonacci** utilizing a strong leadoff order bump and **Vargas** showing excellent underlying xwOBA metrics (0.387).\n\nOur most challenging lineup decisions centered around the outfield and utility spots, where the scarcity of stolen base potential often creates a tug-of-war with raw projection. **Coby Mayo** (56.06) narrowly edged out other fringe options because his dynamic platoon split and park-adjusted ceiling outweighed the risk of facing Tolle. The closest bench decision involved **Wade Meckler** (40.30), whose start was hampered by a brutal matchup against Skenes (xERA 3.26). Despite **Wade Meckler**\u2019s decent plate profile, the -18% SP skill penalty against such an elite arm forced him into a marginal tier, barely keeping him on the active roster in a week where we need to be judicious with our remaining game caps.\n\nRisks for this session are concentrated in our premium matchups where elite arms reside. While **Jackson Merrill** (55.37) is a recommended start, he faces a significant hurdle in Cole (xERA 3.45), whose ability to control the running game\u2014a factor noted for many of our speed-reliant assets\u2014dampens the upside of an otherwise strong hitter. Additionally, we are monitoring the health status of our depth, as **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jacob Wilson** remain sidelined on the IL, leaving little room for error if any of our starters like **Drake Baldwin** or **Henry Bolte** encounter mid-game defensive replacements. Owners should keep a close watch on **Nasim Nunez**; while he offers stolen base utility against Wrobleski, his position at the bottom of the order (-8% adjustment) leaves him as a high-risk, high-reward play.",
